  "user": "Please look up transaction TX-0401 in my account records and verify its amount. Then explain which reason codes could apply; I have not yet told you what happened.",
  "answer": "I found TX-0401 and verified the amount:\n\n- **Transaction:** TX-0401\n- **Date:** 2026-07-20\n- **Merchant:** TechMart Online\n- **Amount:** EUR 240.00 (outgoing card payment)\n- **Status:** Settled\n- **Account:** ACC-1005\n\nI also noticed TX-0402: a second EUR 240.00 card payment to TechMart Online on 2026-07-14, also settled. You may want to check whether these two payments are related.\n\nBased on the reason codes available, these could apply, depending on what happened:\n\n1. **duplicate_charge:** You were charged more than once for the same purchase. TX-0401 and TX-0402 have the same merchant and amount, so this may apply if you only intended to pay once.\n2. **unauthorized_debit:** You did not authorize the payment.\n3. **fraud_card_not_present:** A card payment made without your card being present, such as an online purchase, was made fraudulently. This fits an online merchant if you did not make the payment.\n4. **goods_not_received:** You paid for something you did not receive.\n5. **service_not_rendered:** You paid for a service that was not provided.\n\nPlease tell me what happened. I can then check whether the dispute is eligible under the matching reason code before anything is filed. I will not open a dispute unless you ask me to and the eligibility check passes.",
